  "answer": "### Short Answer\n\n### Interpretation\nUnder Section 84 of the NIRC, the estate tax is imposed on the transfer of the net estate of a decedent. The TRAIN law simplified the estate tax structure by establishing a single rate of 6% for estates valued above the threshold of ₱5,000,000, which means that estates valued at or below this amount are exempt from estate tax.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nThis change in the estate tax rate under the TRAIN law aims to ease the tax burden on smaller estates while ensuring that larger estates contribute a fair share to government revenues. Executors and heirs should be aware of this threshold when planning estate settlements to avoid unexpected tax liabilities.",
